    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea2bc3d8_016bcc40",
        "filename": "board/malefor/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-16T20:01:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SMP specification indicates that for enter ship mode, 0x34 value changes from 0x0100 to 0x0000. This is opposite the LGC specification.\n\nDoes the SMP specification have an error? You should be able to check by reading this register directly from the battery.  If the battery is operating, register 0x34 should have bit 0x0100 clear.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "bc302f40de2429136f97dbd538a3e21bbc1a77c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5bf3d0f7_0cd170d9",
        "filename": "board/malefor/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1248535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-17T03:32:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Keith,\n\nThe battery is operating, register 0x34 has bit 0x0100 clear.\nSMP Spec should indicate right.\nAction for entering ship mode, D-FET OFF function 0x34 value changes to ”0x0100” from “0x0000”.",
      "parentUuid": "ea2bc3d8_016bcc40",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "bc302f40de2429136f97dbd538a3e21bbc1a77c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c16f0107_cf9e8e81",
        "filename": "board/malefor/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-17T15:57:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the SMP specification is correct, then this represents the state of register 0x34\n\n    Battery is operating: 0x34 \u003d 0x0100\n    Battery is in ship mode: 0x34 \u003d 0x0000\nSo you need to set the disconnect_val to 0x0000 (bit is clear).  This is the EC code that uses disconnect_val\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/heads/master/common/battery_fuel_gauge.c#191",
      "parentUuid": "5bf3d0f7_0cd170d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "bc302f40de2429136f97dbd538a3e21bbc1a77c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1daea22c_5e0810a2",
        "filename": "board/malefor/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1248535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-19T07:35:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The SMP SPEC shows:\n1) Enter shipping mode\nD-FET OFF function 0x34 value changes to ”0x0100” from “0x0000” \n2) Exit shipping mode\nD-FET OFF function 0x34 value changes to “0x0000” from “0x0100”\nThese should indicate that\nBattery is in ship mode: 0x34 \u003d 0x0100\nBattery is operating: 0x34 \u003d 0x0000\nThese should be correct. I double check that the 0x34 value is 0x0100 when the battery is shipping mode, it will be 0x0000 when the battery is operating.\n\nBTW, we should enable macro CONFIG_BATTERY_REVIVE_DISCONNECT, otherwise API battery_get_disconnect_state() will not be called and not to check the 0x34 value in volteer family. \n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/heads/master/common/battery_fuel_gauge.c#163",
      "parentUuid": "c16f0107_cf9e8e81",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "bc302f40de2429136f97dbd538a3e21bbc1a77c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d94adf4_f967b4ba",
        "filename": "board/malefor/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 49,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-21T03:12:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dear Keith,\nThe return value(0x0100) should be right. It would not be 0x0000 after enable shipping mode. \nThe messages below are from OEM Specification for your reference. \n\nTurn OFF D-FET (Enable ship mode)\n1. Write “0x0000” to Battery by 0x34(W)\n2. Write “0x1000” to Battery by 0x34(W)\n3. Turn OFF D-FET and return “0x0100” for 0x34(R)",
      "parentUuid": "1daea22c_5e0810a2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 49,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "bc302f40de2429136f97dbd538a3e21bbc1a77c1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
